    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 10.909,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "a matrix power series A(t) with det(A(t)) not identically zero power series. Normalize to have det(A(t)) = 1. Then A(t) = tγcB + o(tγ) with γ > 0, and c ∈ C∗. Make change of variables in A(t) giving A˜(t) by replacing each tβ by exp(−βγ−1σ)tαβγ−1, where σ = log(c). This comes from the necessity to obtain the image of the term ctγ in the desired form as tα, and it is an automorphism of K fixing C. Then A˜(t) = tαB + o(tα) ∈ V (K) ∩ PSL2(K) and VAL(A˜(t)) = (α,[B]R∗). □"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
